  "body": "## Problem\nA valid legacy save with a stale inner economy marker reaches unvalidated treasury fields and emits GDScript errors. The village renderer also creates detailed nodes for every saved building, including distant houses.\n\n## Repair\nApply only the two existing LUMO fixes from e369facf6651352fe68dbed5c1c8345fe57dd309 and 8873683fbf6e8eba6dd5ebe18da39a7d510cb782, adapted to the current live branch. The outer validated save version selects the schema. Near buildings keep their existing detail and collision; distant buildings use bounded shared geometry. All saved buildings and economy data remain intact. Current SafeArea, HUD, native launch and learning connections are retained.\n\n## Evidence and remaining gate\nOn original905, the schema probe emits two treasury SCRIPT ERRORs despite exit0; scale probe fails18 assertions. The four repaired exact blobs pass schema plus924 actual Godot checks. A real local Mesa renderer passes46 scale checks and writes two original PNGs. All13 bound village dependencies are byte-identical on a7bb. Independent review confirmed original hashes and strict error rejection. Full combined Discovery, Android, signed APK and update checks remain required on the final host source. No physical-device or FPS claim.\n\nNo new third-party code, assets or dependencies. The protected main branch is not targeted.\n\n----\n## Summary by Gitar\n\n- **Export packaging:**\n    - Added existing attribution notices to the Android export `include_filter` in `export_presets.cfg`\n- **Asset manifest:**\n    - Removed stale `models` entries in `assets/manifests/assets.json` and documented the empty categories\n- **Village HUD:**\n    - Added compact landscape layout in `build_settlement_world.gd` that reparents existing labels and scroll lists into columns\n- **Plot selection:**\n    - Plot picking uses the camera far distance, and the planning camera fits the 3x3 starting footprint\n\n<sub>This will update automatically on new commits.</sub>",
